{% doc %}
  Currency selector popover. Rendered next to its trigger inside `.js-markets-
  wrap` — usually twice per header (once in the desktop chrome and once in the
  mobile drawer-extras) so the dropdown can absolute-anchor to whichever
  trigger opened it. Driven by a self-contained toggle controller in
  `index.ts`; intentionally NOT wired into the shared offcanvas machinery so
  opening the dropdown from inside the mobile nav drawer never closes the
  drawer. Selections auto-submit the localization form, which reloads the
  page on the new market.

  The allow-list accepts country ISO codes (US, CA, …) plus a special `EUR`
  entry that adds one row with the EU flag (`assets/eur-flag.png`) and submits
  the first available EUR market country.

  @param {string} allowed_countries - Optional. Comma/newline-separated ISO

  country codes (plus optional `EUR`) controlling which rows show and in what order. Blank shows all available countries
  in Shopify order.
{% enddoc %}

{% liquid
  assign selected_country = localization.country
  assign selected_currency = localization.country.currency.iso_code | upcase
  assign country_found = false

  for country in localization.available_countries
    if country.iso_code == localization.country.iso_code
      assign country_found = true
    endif
  endfor

  if country_found == false
    for country in localization.available_countries
      if country.iso_code == 'US'
